  "document": "William Garwood\nWilliam Davis Garwood, Jr.( April 28, 1884 – December 28, 1950) was an American stage and film actor and director of the early silent film era in the 1910s. Between 1911 and 1913, Garwood starred in a number of early adaptions of popular films, including\" Jane Eyre\" and\" The Vicar of Wakefield\"( 1910),\" Lorna Doone\"( 1911),\" The Pied Piper of Hamelin\"( 1911),\" David Copperfield\"( 1911),\" The Merchant of Venice\"( 1912), and\" Little Dorrit\"( 1913), and\" Robin Hood\"( 1913). In total, he starred in more than 150 short and feature films."
